nd variable invoice due dates (60, 45, and 30 days from date of payment capture) for pre-approved spending amounts (“Net Terms Credits”), which may be provided to each individual Buyer based on Buyer’s credit score, financial information, purchasing history on FASHIONGO, and other factors. Buyer agrees that Buyer will not create multiple accounts in an attempt to increase Buyer’s Net Terms Credits or circumvent these Terms of Service. FASHIONGO reserves the right to modify or terminate Buyer’s Dynamic Net Terms and/or suspend or revoke Buyer’s eligibility to use Dynamic Net Terms at any time, without prior notice, and based on its sole discretion.<br><br>Buyers will undergo Balance’s onboarding qualification and activation flows, or as otherwise required by Balance, which will determine their eligibility to use Dynamic Net Terms at checkout. This may include disclosing business and financial details and adding a backup payment method (“Net Terms Card”).</p><dl><dt>Payment with Dynamic Net Terms</dt><dd><strong>Full Terms and Partial Terms</strong> (Split Payment Method). FASHIONGO and Balance offer Dynamic Net Terms in two forms: a) full terms; and b) partial terms. Full terms refer to the payment of an order made entirely with Net Terms Credits. Partial terms, or “Split Payment Method,” refer to the payment of an order made partially with Net Terms Credits. The order’s remaining amount is charged to the Net Terms Card (“Spot Payment”). The transaction date will be identical for Net Terms and Net Terms Card on every order. Buyers will not be able to use Dynamic Net Terms as a payment method option at checkout if the Available Net Terms is less than $20 USD.<br><br>The Split Payment Method may be used: 1) if the amount at Buyer’s checkout exceeds the Available Net Terms; or 2) if the amount at Buyer’s checkout is less than the Available Net Terms, but additional costs (such as additional fees or the addition of extra products) make it so that the order grand total exceeds the Available Net Terms. The Split Payment Method may only be used for orders that meet the minimum transaction amount ($1 USD).<br><br><strong>Checkout</strong>. At order checkout, Buyer will be presented with two payment options: 1) credit/debit card; or 2) Dynamic Net Terms. If Buyer opts to use Dynamic Net Terms, Balance will run a temporary authorization hold in the amount of $1 USD on the selected Net Terms Card. The temporary authorization hold will be removed upon Balance’s verification of the Net Terms Card.<br><br>Buyer is required to have a Net Terms Card on file upon checkout to cover any potential remaining amount or related service fees. In the event that there is more than one Net Terms Card on file, the default order in which the Net Terms Card is used will vary.<br><br>The Net Terms Card that was used during checkout will be charged for the Net Terms invoice for the order and the Spot Payment portion (if applicable).<br><br>The order grand total may be different from the checkout amount due to additional fees (e.g., shipping fees, handling fees, etc.), applied discounts, updated item quantities (added or deleted), and updated item(s) (e.g. to reflect backorder status).<br><br>In the event that the selected Net Terms Card is declined at a vendor’s order payment capture, vendors will be notified of declined “pending” card status. Subsequently, Buyer’s entire order will be put on hold and the Net Terms Credits used on the order will remain as “reserved” until the declined card issue is resolved.<br><br><strong>Net Terms Credits and Available Net Terms</strong>. Any available Net Terms Credits will be applied to the order before Split Payment Method is utilized (e.g., if there is any remaining amount that exceeds the current Net Terms Credit balance). Store credits cannot be used on Dynamic Net Terms orders.<br><br>The amount of Net Terms Credits for which Buyer has been preapproved is referred to as the Available Net Terms (“Available Net Terms”). Buyer’s Available Net Terms reserves, or sets aside, Net Terms Credits for new or confirmed orders for which payment has not yet been captured. These reserved Net Terms Credits are allocated toward the order until the invoice payment is completed.  By way of example, if the Split Payment Method was automatically applied at order checkout due to insufficient Available Net Terms, with $30 paid in Net Terms Credits and $20 paid with the Net Terms Card, then $30 worth of Net Terms Credits would be deducted from Buyer’s total Available Net Terms until the invoice payment is completed. The $20 paid with the Net Terms Card would be immediately processed at vendor’s order payment capture.<br><br>Upon Buyer’s order checkout, Net Terms Credits used for that particular order will be subtracted from Buyer’s overall Available Net Terms. Buyer’s Available Net Terms will update in real time, reflecting changes immediately as transactions occur due to order checkout, adjustment, refund, cancellation, and paid invoices. When Buyer makes a payment on net terms invoices, the payment amount will be added back to their Available Net Terms. This will apply instantly upon payment confirmation. Available Net Terms will then automatically apply to orders in chronological order for net terms status (reserved by buyer checkout or captured by vendor payment capture, whichever comes first). Buyer can refer to their Available Net Terms in multiple locations, such as at payment method selection during checkout and at Payment Activity on the My Dynamic Net Terms page.<br><br>There may be instances in which Buyer will be unable to use Net Terms Credits upon order checkout (e.g., Buyer’s Available Net Terms is below $20 USD; Buyer selects “FG Consolidated Shipping” for the order’s shipping method; etc.). If Net Terms Credits are disabled as a payment method, Buyer will not be able to use Net Terms Credits toward their order. FASHIONGO, at its sole discretion, reserves the right to revoke Buyer’s ability to use Net Terms Credits upon order checkout, and to modify the circumstances in which Net Terms Credits may or may not be used.<br><br><strong>Refunds</strong>. In the event of a refund, the amount paid via Net Terms Credits will be refunded first and will be refunded in the form of Net Terms Credits. If applicable, such as in the event that Split Payment Method was used at checkout, any remaining amount will be made to Buyer’s Net Terms Card. Refunds on orders utilizing Net Terms will follow the same process as the itemized refund.<br><br><strong>Net Terms Card</strong>. Buyer is required to enter a Net Terms Card as a part of Balance’s activation flow. Buyer is required to have a Net Terms Card on file upon checkout to act as a backup payment method and cover any potential remaining amount or related service fees, and to be available for invoice payments made in advance or on the invoice due date. There are no payment due dates for transactions made with Net Terms Card, as the payment is charged immediately upon capture.<br><br>In the event that the Net Terms Card or other chosen payment method declines, Buyer must manually resolve by selecting another method of payment.<br><br><strong>Payment Flexibility</strong>. Buyers can either pay an invoice in advance or on the due date by auto-charge via Balance or in advance by accessing Pay Now to Balance on the FASHIONGO platform. To make the payment in advance, Buyer must manually pay the invoice on FASHIONGO’s Dynamic Net Terms menu. If Buyer opts to make the payment on the due date of the invoice, Buyer’s selected payment method will be automatically charged upon that date.<dt>Late Payment.</dt><dd>In the event that Buyer has not yet paid the invoice(s) past the due date, Buyer will receive a notification from Balance and/or FASHIONGO alerting Buyer to do so. FASHIONGO and/or Balance reserves the right to impose fees due to late invoice payment with notice. The fee rate and amount will be disclosed to Buyers in advance.</dd><dt>Credit History Access.</dt><dd>Buyer authorizes Balance and its authorized third-party partner to access Buyer’s personal and business credit card history, including obtaining a consumer credit report, in order to evaluate Buyer’s eligibility in opening a line of credit with Balance. <br><br><strong>Indemnification.</strong> Buyer will defend, indemnify, and hold harmless FASHIONGO, its parent company, its affiliates, and their respective directors, officers, employees, representatives, agents, successors, and assigns from and against any and all claims, demands, losses, liabilities, costs, expenses, and damages including legal fees, arising out of a) any actual or alleged breach of any term of these Terms of Service by Buyer; b) or any negligence, breach of contract, misrepresentation, or tort by Buyer; c) Buyer’s violation of any applicable law; or d) any breach or violation of Balance’s terms or agreements by Buyer.</dd><dt>Disclaimer of Warranty and Limitation of Liability.</dt><dd>By utilizing Dynamic Net Terms, Buyer agrees to release and hold harmless FASHIONGO, its affiliates and subsidiaries, parent company, directors, officers, employees, and agents, and any other entity associated with Dynamic Net Terms to user (collectively, the “Released Parties”) from any and all claims, loss, or damages arising out of, or in connection with Dynamic Net Terms. THERE ARE NO REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO STATUTORY WARRANTIES AND CONDITIONS, WARRANTIES AND CONDITIONS OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, THIRD PARTIES RIGHTS, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT OF PROPRIETARY RIGHTS. IN NO EVENT WILL FASHIONGO BE LIABLE TO ANY PARTY FOR ANY CONSEQUENTIAL, INCIDENTAL, INDIRECT, PUNITIVE, EXEMPLARY, OR SPECIAL DAMAGES, INCLUDING ANY LOST PROFITS, HOWEVER CAUSED AND REGARDLESS OF THEORY OR LIABILITY.  FASHIONGO’s liability for direct damages in connection with Dynamic Net Terms shall in no event exceed the greater of 1) the total of any fees paid or collected in the six months prior to the date of the initial claim made against FASHIONGO or 2) US $100.00.</dd><dt>Governing Law.</dt><dd>If any provision of these Terms of Service is deemed unlawful, void, or for any reason unenforceable, then that provision will be deemed severable from these Terms of Service and will not affect the validity and enforceability of any remaining provisions. The laws of the State of California, without reference to conflict of law rules, govern these Terms of Service.</dd><dt>Superseding Terms.</dt><dd>Notwithstanding anything to the contrary herein, the terms of FASHIONGO’s Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, and Buyer Services Agreement shall prevail over these Terms of Service to the extent there is any inconsistency in terms between these Terms of Service and FASHIONGO’s Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, and Buyer Services Agreement.</dd><dt>Contact Us.</dt><dd>For any questions related to orders, contact FASHIONGO at info@fashiongo.net. For any questions related to Dynamic Net Terms payments or invoices, contact Balance at support@getbalance.com.</dd></dl></div>')}a.__dustBody=!0;return a}(dust));(function(M){M.register(\"NewCatMenuTl\",L);function L(V,U){return V.w('<!-- category : new arrival --><div class=\"filter open\"><button class=\"tit nclick\" data-nclick-name=\"').f(U.get([\"fromPage\"],false),U,\"h\").w('.left.hidecate\" data-nclick-id=\"2\"><span>').f(U.get([\"titleMenu\"],false),U,\"h\").w('</span></button><ul class=\"nav_category\">').s(U.get([\"topMenu\"],false),U,{block:K},{}).w(\"</ul></div><!-- //category : new arrival -->\")}L.__dustBody=!0;function K(V,U){return V.h(\"if\",U,{block:J},{cond:k},\"h\")}K.__dustBody=!0;function J(V,U){return V.w(\"<li \").s(U.get([\"onCategoryArray\"],false),U,{block:H},{onCid:U.get([\"cid\"],false)}).w('><div class=\"mn\"><span class=\"nclick chk ').s(U.get([\"onCategoryArray\"],false),U,{block:A},{onCid:U.get([\"cid\"],false)}).w('\" id=\"').f(U.get([\"cid\"],f